# Cursor Rules for Audit Workspace

This file mirrors conventions from CLAUDE.md for use in the Cursor IDE.

## Quick Reference

**Stack:** Next.js 14+, TypeScript (strict), MUI v6. No Tailwind or shadcn.

**State:** Single `useReducer` for domain data. UI state stays local. Filter results computed with `useMemo`, never stored.

**Styling:** MUI `sx` prop only. All colors from theme tokens. No CSS files.

**Components:** Presentational components receive callbacks, never dispatch directly. Activity logged on every domain mutation.

**Types:** Interfaces for objects, types for unions. Named exports everywhere.

**Dates:** Parse YYYY-MM-DD as local with `new Date(y, m-1, d)` to avoid timezone bugs.

**Copy:** Professional, no exclamation marks, sentence case. Action descriptions follow "[Verb] [object] [preposition] [context]" pattern.

See CLAUDE.md for full context; see .claude/skills/ for detailed guidance on MUI, state, and domain vocabulary.
